# fixtures/hex/fragments/anchors/records.hex: anchor records ([F08 §10.3]) of the forms the stores do not hold, back to
# back; decode as anchor records to the end of the file. The stores' anchors (quote, range with a marker, file,
# lines, a repinned quote) are in fixtures/hex/store-a. Here: kind 2 `heading` with a Markdown scope and kind 3
# `symbol` with a Rust scope, as an import keeps them ([F08 §10.3.1]: no writer captures either under the interim
# scanner rule, an imported anchor keeps its bytes); a hash-only `quote` and a hash-only `range` (text_unavailable,
# with quote_h, prefix_h, suffix_h and end_h, [40 §5.7]); an anchor with a predecessor term and an occurrence index;
# and a `file` anchor of a planned target (blob algo `none`). captured values are synthetic (an imported anchor's
# captured is trusted, [F08 §11.5]); each uid is the anchor derivation of [F08 §11.4] over the synthetic source uid
# BLAKE3-128("moirai-fixture:anchors/src"), captured and pred. Window values follow [F20 §2.7.3].

